{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The Secret Valentine", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Roses Are Red", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " To Be Supposed To", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future. <br /><br /> The structure is: <br /><br /> Subject + To be + supposed to + verb <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">When you take an escalator you are supposed to stand right, walk left. <br /><br /></span>  **Pronunciation tip**:<br /> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br /><br /> Like this:<br /> Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "That's supposed to be a hip neighborhood these days! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Every girl felt like she was supposed to get a red rose from someone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " People in England are supposed to be very polite. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you take an escalator you are supposed to stand right, walk left.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you meet someone are you supposed to shake their hand?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Modals For Suggestion, Necessity and Possibility", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Modals are auxiliary verbs used to make suggestions, express necessity or show possibility. In the simple present you need a modal plus the base form of the main verb.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":13,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">    Modals of Suggestion    </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Should \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You should try to find cheap accommodations. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Ought to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  You ought to find a cheap hotel.   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">   You couldn't try to find cheap accommodations.   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">    Modals of Necessity     </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">   You mustn't jump the queue.    </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Had better\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">   You had better not jump the queue.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Have to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">   You have to wait in a queue.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">   Modals of Possibility  </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"May\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">  There may be more public displays of affection than usual!   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You might see people kissing!   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You could go to Brick Lane  </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Things to remember: <ul> \t<li> You do not use ought to in the negative form!</li> <li>When you use could in the negative form it changes its function from suggestion to impossibility. </li><li>The meaning of <span class=\"italic\">have to changes if it is negative. Don't have to means that it is not necessary. </li> </ul>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "escalator ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a moving staircase", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When you take an escalator you are supposed to stand right, walk left.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about customs and manners. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "queue ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a line of people or cars waiting", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You mustn't jump the queue.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "public displays of affection", "type": "name"}, {"content": "physical affection shown in front of others", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There may be more public displays of affection than usual!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le13ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to drop the subject ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to stop talking about a particular subject", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's drop the subject 